FujiNet Go Apple II (desktop) -- rolling notes
==============================================

Follows the 10-step order of work in fujinet-go-adam-desktop/PORTING.md §12.

Done (this pass)
----------------

M1 -- core + GNOME frontend, emulator half only:

* Repo skeleton, GPL-3.0, two pinned submodules:
    third_party/applewin           FujiNetWIFI/AppleWin @ 25e8ddd (branch linux)
    third_party/fujinet-firmware   FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-firmware @ 7a994ab
* cmake/Dependencies.cmake -- apple2_provide_dependency(), 3-step resolution
  (<NAME>_SRC override -> submodule -> clone the pin), sentinel files, pin
  drift warning.
* cmake/StageAppleWin.cmake -- copies source/resource/libyaml/minizip/bin
  into core/applewin-generated (file(COPY), not rsync: Windows), then runs
  tools/applewin/patch-staged-tree.py through ${Python3_EXECUTABLE}. MSYS2
  CMake cannot execute_process a .sh, but a native python is fine.
  .source-info records the source commit + a hash of the patch script, so
  editing a transform re-stages. -DAPPLEWIN_RESTAGE=ON forces it.
* tools/applewin/patch-staged-tree.py -- the 13 transforms, ported from the
  Android build-applewin-core.sh. All idempotent, all hard-fail on a missing
  anchor. NOTE: the idempotency test must check the REPLACEMENT before the
  anchor -- several transforms wrap their anchor rather than replacing it, so
  anchor-first re-applies them (nested Boost if(), duplicated slot7 block).
* core/ -- libapple2session:
    applewin/apple2_host.{cpp,h}  the libretro frontend, ported from Android
                                  (android/log.h replaced by a log-sink seam)
    src/session.c                 paced emulator thread, vsync phase-lock
    src/input_map.c               X11 keysym -> libretro (keycode, char, mods)
    src/{settings,paths,audio_sdl,gamepad_sdl,fujinet_runtime}.c
  Differences from the ADAM target, all deliberate:
    - frames are XRGB8888 uint32, not RGB565
    - geometry is NOT fixed: copy_frame reports w/h, because a VidHD card in
      slot 3 switches the core between 560x384 and 640x400
    - audio is interleaved stereo, not mono (FujiNet's SAM overlay is mono and
      is mixed into both channels)
    - the joystick is a pair of analog paddles, not a digital stick
* frontends/gnome -- GTK4 + libadwaita, XRGB8888 straight into a
  GdkMemoryTexture (no per-pixel conversion), aspect TV 4:3 / square / integer,
  preferences over the shared settings store.
  NOTE: Alt is NOT passed to the window manager here (unlike the ADAM
  frontend) -- the Alt keys are Open Apple and Closed Apple.
* ctest: input (key + paddle mapping), boot_smoke (headless core boot),
  desktop_entry_gnome, metainfo_gnome. All passing.
* COMPLIANCE.md.

Verified: Enhanced Apple //e boots to its banner in the GNOME window at
60 fps with 60/60 frames on vsync (APPLE2_PACE_LOG=1).

Findings worth remembering
--------------------------

* The AppleWin libretro core's DEFAULT video_mode is "Color (RGB Card/Monitor)",
  which emulates an RGB card. With no such card fitted it renders a blank text
  screen as blue horizontal banding instead of black -- the boot screen is
  unreadable, and it looks exactly like a framebuffer/stride bug. Every other
  mode renders correctly. We default to "Color (Composite Monitor)" and expose
  the setting. Worth reporting upstream.
* createRetroRegistry() returns an EMPTY registry, so anything not covered by
  a core option falls back to AppleWin's internal default. There is no slot6
  core option, so the Disk ][ in slot 6 is not configurable from here.
* DebugGetVideoMode() returns the *debugger's* video-mode override, not the
  machine's -- it leaves the output untouched when the debugger is inactive.
  Use Video::GetVideoMode() via GetVideo() to read the real one.

M2 -- clone-and-build verified two ways:
  * a plain `git clone` (no --recurse-submodules) auto-fetches the submodules
    and builds; ctest green.
  * a tree with .git and third_party/* removed takes the clone-the-pin branch
    of apple2_provide_dependency and builds; ctest green.

M3 -- FujiNet in-process. THE BUS IS UP; CONFIG DOES NOT BOOT YET.

  Working:
  * tools/fujinet/build-fujinet-desktop.sh forked from adam's, PC_TARGET=APPLE,
    [BOIP] port=1985, web UI 8000. All 11 target-independent patch blocks kept;
    the two ADAM portability patches replaced by the two APPLE ones
    (fnFsSPIFFS.cpp + mgHttpClient.cpp root their paths absolutely from
    FUJINET_RUNTIME_ROOT, because AppleWin's SetCurrentImageDir() chdir()s and
    moves the shared process CWD out from under FujiNet). Builds first try.
  * libfujinet.so exports exactly the six-symbol contract, 8 symbols total --
    the ELF version script is doing its job.
  * The runtime loads in-process, mounts SPIFFS and SD from absolute paths,
    reads our fnconfig.ini, mounts /autorun.po, and attaches to the bus.
  * SmartPort/SLIP is live: LISTEN 127.0.0.1:1985 plus an ESTABLISHED pair
    whose BOTH endpoints belong to our own PID, with iwm_slip::encode_packet
    traffic and "handling init command" / "Sending INIT Response Packet".

  Two real defects found and fixed along the way:
  * The AppleWin libretro frontend NEVER STARTS THE SLIP LISTENER. Upstream
    starts it in LoadConfiguration() and in the Windows property sheet; the
    libretro path reaches neither, and the card ctor only logs. FujiNet dials
    forever and nothing answers. Staging patch 13 starts it from the
    SmartPortOverSlip constructor -- inserting the card is when its listener
    should come up, and patch 8/9 already makes start() safe over a previous
    listener. Patch 14 changes default_listener_address to 127.0.0.1: upstream
    binds 0.0.0.0, which exposes an unauthenticated block-device channel to
    the network, and the default is what LoadConfiguration re-initialises from.
    BOTH BELONG UPSTREAM.
  * Startup order is the OPPOSITE of ADAM's, and it is not cosmetic. FujiNet's
    APPLE build blocks inside setup (iwm_slip::setup_spi) until the SLIP
    connection is made. Starting it first (as adam does) deadlocks the whole
    session: start_runtime never returns, the emulator thread is never created,
    the listener never binds, and FujiNet waits forever. The session now starts
    the emulator, waits on a condvar for the core to report itself up, and only
    then starts FujiNet. The Android app does the same. PORTING.md §2 lists
    Apple2 as having "forgiving" ordering like ADAM -- that is wrong, and the
    guide is worth correcting.

  NOT working -- the next thing to do:
  * The machine sits at the "Apple //e" banner and never boots FujiNet CONFIG,
    even though the SmartPort dialogue is happening. Leads:
      - the INIT response reports "status: 255, num: 0" and enumerates drives
        as unit 0d/0e, which looks wrong for a first device;
      - check whether the //e autostart actually enters the slot-7 spoverslip
        firmware, or falls through to the Disk ][ in slot 6 (before the card
        was inserted the CPU sat at $C65E, inside that ROM);
      - a post-connect cold reset was tried and does NOT fix it;
      - compare the SmartPort dialogue against the known-good standalone
        fujinet-pc-apple2 driving a real AppleWin (sa2) build.
  * fnconfig.ini is still the Android app's ATARI default (hsioindex,
    [Cassette], enable_apetime, Atari TNFS hosts). Curate it for Apple II.
  * Web UI port 8000 collides with a standalone fujinet-pc-atari on this
    machine; FUJINET_WEBUI_BIND overrides it for testing.

Next
----
M4  settings, media import, ROM import (needed for WITH_APPLE_ROMS=OFF --
    see COMPLIANCE.md; currently OFF is a hard error), gamepad, audio.
M5  KDE frontend (early, to keep the core toolkit-agnostic).
M6  debugger engine + first native window. Investigate the single-step seam
    EARLY: AppleWin executes per-cycle inside executeOneFrame() and there is
    no ready single-instruction entry point at the libretro boundary. Stage
    the read-only views first so the debugger is useful even if stepping is
    late. Symbols are free -- bin/*.SYM are already staged.
M7  CI: linux, then macOS and Windows, then flatpak.
    Top Windows risk: the AppleWin libretro frontend has never been built
    under MinGW (the cross-compile work upstream covers the SDL2 frontend).
M8  icons (art is in ~/Workspace/fujinet-go-launchers/ic_launcher_APPLE2),
    desktop entries, AppStream, screenshots.
M9  flatpak (Boost headers must be a declared module -- the GNOME/KDE SDKs do
    not ship them), NSIS, release job.
M10 macOS + Windows frontends and their debugger windows.
